# =============================================================================
# 030-no-ai.patch — PyreVixen: generative AI features default-off / removed
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
#   Disables every AI code path that exists in this tree:
#   1. The only AI Nimbus feature, `shake-to-summarize`, defaults to
#      enabled=false on every channel (was true on developer/nightly/beta).
#   2. No AI features are registered in Components.aiFeatureRegistry
#      (PageSummaryFeature and VoiceSearchAIControlFeature registrations
#      deleted). With an empty registry the AI Controls settings screen lists
#      nothing and no AI feature can run.
#
# VERIFIED AGAINST: FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0_RELEASE (2026-10-14).
#   * Real AI surface in Fenix 158 (no chatbot sidebar exists in this tree —
#     verified: zero "chatbot" hits in fenix/app/src/main/java):
#       - Components.aiFeatureRegistry (components/Components.kt:499):
#         AIFeatureRegistry.default(...).also { register(PageSummaryFeature);
#         register(VoiceSearchAIControlFeature) }
#       - Components.aiControlsFeatureBlock (Components.kt:514): the built-in
#         global AI kill-switch UI (AIFeatureBlock, storage default not blocked).
#       - Components.llm (Components.kt:523): MLPA LLM client, consumed only by
#         SummarizationFragment (requireComponents.llm.mlpaProvider).
#       - Nimbus feature `shake-to-summarize` (nimbus.fml.yaml:214), which feeds
#         Settings.shakeToSummarizeFeatureFlagEnabled (utils/Settings.kt:2768).
#   * There are NO browser.ml.* prefs in mobile/android/app/geckoview-prefs.js
#     (the first draft's pref list was invented for the desktop pref space).
#     browser.ml.* keys remain enforceable via config/default-prefs.js if Gecko
#     ever honours them on Android, but no code change can target them here.
#   * Entry points to the summary UI (browser menu item, shake gesture) are
#     gated on the feature flags this patch turns off
#     (SummarizationNavigator.navigateToSummarizationIfEligible checks
#     featureEnabled; BrowserFragment gates the gesture on
#     summarizeFeatureSettings.canShowFeature), so the unreachable UI and the
#     `llm` client remain in the tree as dead code.
#
# DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE FIRST DRAFT
#   * The invented nimbus.fml.yaml feature stubs (chatbot / ai-tab-grouping /
#     page-summarization) are dropped: only `shake-to-summarize` really exists.
#   * The invented Components.kt "ChatbotController" hunk is replaced with the
#     real aiFeatureRegistry registration block.
#   * The invented browser.ml.* pref list is dropped (no such keys in this
#     tree's geckoview-prefs.js).
#
# CONFIDENCE
#   * Both hunks CONFIDENT — contexts copied verbatim from the 158.0 tree,
#     verified with `git apply --check`.
#   * Follow-up (not in this patch): deleting the now-dead Summarization*
#     UI, the `llm` client, and the ai-controls registry classes entirely.
#     Post-build check: the Settings "AI" entry shows no features, and no
#     network traffic goes to any MLPA/AI endpoint.
# =============================================================================

diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml b/mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml
index 4d1ddfb..2166a48 100644
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml
@@ -217,17 +217,18 @@ features:
       enabled:
         type: Boolean
         description: If true, shake to summarize will be enabled
-        default: true
+        # PYREVIXEN: AI summarization is disabled on all channels.
+        default: false
     defaults:
       - channel: developer
         value:
-          enabled: true
+          enabled: false
       - channel: nightly
         value:
-          enabled: true
+          enabled: false
       - channel: beta
         value:
-          enabled: true
+          enabled: false
 
   weekly-privacy-notification:
     description: A feature that shows a recurring weekly notification summarizing Tracking Protection activity.
diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt
